<% content_for :page_title, "Canadiana Collection - #{application_name}" %>

<div class="home-page">
  <section class="site-section about-intro about-intro--canadiana">
    <div class="canadiana-shell about-intro-grid about-intro-grid--canadiana">
      <div class="about-intro-copy about-intro-copy--canadiana">
        <h1 class="section-title">Canadiana Collection</h1>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Approximately 31 million pages of publications that show how knowledge, stories, and information were shared over time.
          This collection includes books, newspapers, magazines, government documents, maps, and more from c. 1500 to the present day.
          Canadiana content is largely drawn from the Canadian Institute for Historic Micro-reproductions (CIHM) microfiche series.
        </p>
      </div>
      <%= render partial: 'shared/canadiana_stack', locals: { count: 12, collection: :canadiana } %>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="site-section about-modern-section about-modern-section--canadiana">
  <div class="canadiana-shell about-modern-layout">
    <div class="about-modern-feature-grid">
      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--copy">
        <h2>31 million pages in one collection</h2>
        <p>
          Browse materials spanning approximately five centuries of Canadian publishing, from early imprints to twentieth-century
          periodicals and documents.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--media">
        <img src="<%= asset_path('monog.jpg') %>" alt="Historic books and publications from the Canadiana Collection" loading="lazy">
      </article>
      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--media">
        <img src="<%= asset_path('maps.jpg') %>" alt="Historic map materials from the Canadiana Collection" loading="lazy">
      </article>
      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--copy">
        <h2>Collection depth built for serious research</h2>
        <p>
          Content includes books, newspapers, magazines, maps, and government publications selected through expert advisory
          guidance and sustained digitization partnerships.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="about-modern-block about-modern-deep-dive" aria-labelledby="canadiana-deep-dive-title">
      <div class="about-modern-block-head">
        <h2 id="canadiana-deep-dive-title">What you can find in the Canadiana Collection</h2>
      </div>

      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--detail about-modern-card--detail-books" aria-labelledby="canadiana-detail-books-title">
        <header class="about-modern-detail-header">
          <h3 id="canadiana-detail-books-title">Books and Publications</h3>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-intro">
            The Books and Publications collection, spanning three and a half centuries of Canadian documentary history, holds rich
            primary materials exploring a wide range of subjects and disciplines. With a projected 84,000 titles by completion,
            this resource is the most comprehensive full-text searchable set of historical books and publications currently
            available for the study of Canada. Topics range from major historical events to the development of institutions,
            laws and science; from Canadian literature to philosophical treatises; from agriculture to politics, trade and tariffs.
          </p>
          <div class="about-modern-detail-metadata" role="list" aria-label="Books and Publications summary">
            <p class="about-modern-detail-size" role="listitem">
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-label">Size</span>
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-value">84,000 titles</span>
            </p>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Coverage to 1920</span>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">47 languages</span>
          </div>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-criteria">
            <strong>Selection criteria:</strong> Books and Publications contains Canadian imprints (monographs and pamphlets) to
            1920. In addition, selected works published outside the country, either by Canadian authors or relating to Canada,
            were included for digitization. An advisory board composed of scholars and library collection specialists established
            and guided collection development efforts.
          </p>
        </header>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-grid">
          <section class="about-modern-detail-panel">
            <h4>Contents</h4>
            <p>
              Books and Publications is comprehensive, with titles selected and digitized from the holdings of more than 200 libraries.
              Between 2003 and 2016, Canadiana strengthened and updated this research collection by adding monograph titles identified
              and located by scholars as well as by titles recently acquired by major Canadian repositories. Onsite surveys of
              libraries, archives, and uncatalogued special collections have brought to light both rare and previously unknown imprints.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section class="about-modern-detail-panel">
            <h4>Collection Highlights</h4>
            <ul class="about-modern-detail-list">
              <li>All Books and Publications microfilmed by the Canadian Institute for Historical Microreproductions (CIHM)</li>
              <li>All Books and Publications available on Early Canadiana Online (ECO)</li>
              <li>Recently digitized Books and Publications never before published by Canadiana</li>
              <li>Areas of collection strength include women's history, Indigenous history, exploration and anthropology, immigration, Canadian literature, genealogy and local history, military history, law, politics, and medicine</li>
              <li>Religion occupied a major place in 19th century society and publishing, a fact reflected in the breadth of religious publications collected within</li>
              <li>Titles in 47 different languages, including in 14 Indigenous languages</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-footer">
          <a class="about-modern-detail-link" href="/catalog?f%5Bcollection_tsim_str%5D%5B%5D=Monographs+%7C+Monographies&amp;q=&amp;search_field=all_fields&amp;lang=<%= I18n.locale %>">Browse Books and Publications</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--detail about-modern-card--detail-serials" aria-labelledby="canadiana-detail-serials-title">
        <header class="about-modern-detail-header">
          <h3 id="canadiana-detail-serials-title">Newspapers and Magazines</h3>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-intro">
            The Newspapers and Magazines collection includes a wide range of dailies, weeklies, specialized journals and
            mass-market magazines, as well as city directories and annual reports from churches, schools, and corporations.
            Specialized publications include trade or industry journals in addition to popular magazines catering to various
            demographics: men, women, students, children, and diverse ethnolinguistic communities. Early periodicals are an
            invaluable source of information for researchers in all fields, as they offer a remarkable record of thought and
            opinion on diverse issues facing society. Lavishly illustrated journals open a captivating window onto early Canadian
            society and culture through their articles, advertisements, cartoons, drawings and photographs.
          </p>
          <div class="about-modern-detail-metadata" role="list" aria-label="Newspapers and Magazines summary">
            <p class="about-modern-detail-size" role="listitem">
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-label">Size</span>
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-value">1,700 periodical titles, plus annuals and newspapers</span>
            </p>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Annuals to 1900</span>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Periodicals to 1920</span>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Newspapers to 1930</span>
          </div>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-criteria">
            <strong>Selection criteria:</strong> Newspapers and Magazines contains annuals up to 1900, periodicals up to 1920 and
            newspapers up to 1930. The periodicals subset draws heavily on the Early Canadian Periodicals project, which worked
            closely with an Advisory Committee to determine the collection parameters and scanning priorities.
          </p>
        </header>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-grid about-modern-detail-grid--single">
          <section class="about-modern-detail-panel">
            <h4>Collection Highlights</h4>
            <ul class="about-modern-detail-list">
              <li>All annuals and periodicals microfilmed by the Canadian Institute for Historical Microreproductions (CIHM)</li>
              <li>All periodicals available on Early Canadiana Online (ECO)</li>
              <li>Newspapers and Magazines recently added to our collection and are not available on ECO or in the CIHM fiche collection</li>
              <li>Local, trade, religious, and student newspapers and journals</li>
              <li>City directories and annual reports from churches, schools, businesses and other organizations</li>
              <li>Specialized periodicals devoted to a wide range of topics: literature, medicine, science and technology, education, agriculture, business, recreation and sports, politics, religion, history, law, the military, music, genealogy, books and publishing, economics, fashion, philately, photography, humour, psychology, transportation, etc.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-footer">
          <a class="about-modern-detail-link" href="/catalog?f%5Bcollection_tsim_str%5D%5B%5D=Serials+%7C+Publications+en+se%CC%81rie&amp;q=&amp;search_field=all_fields&amp;lang=<%= I18n.locale %>">Browse Newspapers and Magazines</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--detail about-modern-card--detail-government" aria-labelledby="canadiana-detail-government-title">
        <header class="about-modern-detail-header">
          <h3 id="canadiana-detail-government-title">Government Publications</h3>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-intro">
            The Government Publications collection includes over 1.7 million pages of historical pre-1900 colonial, provincial and
            federal government documents. This collection includes government acts, bills, committee reports, court rules, debates,
            journals, ordinances, a selection of official publications from France and Great Britain, sessional papers, regulations,
            royal commission reports, voter's lists and treaties.
          </p>
          <div class="about-modern-detail-metadata" role="list" aria-label="Government Publications summary">
            <p class="about-modern-detail-size" role="listitem">
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-label">Size</span>
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-value">8,500 books and publications; 79 series titles</span>
            </p>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Pre-1900 focus</span>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">Colonial and federal records</span>
          </div>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-criteria">
            <strong>Selection criteria:</strong> Government Publications is the fruit of the Early Official Publications project,
            whose parameters were set by the Government Publications Advisory Committee. Municipal government publications and
            post-Confederation provincial publications are not included in this collection.
          </p>
        </header>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-grid about-modern-detail-grid--single">
          <section class="about-modern-detail-panel">
            <h4>Collection Highlights</h4>
            <ul class="about-modern-detail-list">
              <li>A selection of pre-Confederation official government publications produced by colonial legislatures, such as acts, legislative debates, legislative journals, and sessional papers</li>
              <li>A selection of federal government documents published 1867-1900, such as acts, parliamentary debates, parliamentary journals, royal commission reports and sessional papers</li>
              <li>Pre-1900 publications from France and Great Britain that relate to the governance of Canada, such as treaties, acts, bills, correspondence, British Parliamentary papers and reports</li>
              <li>Civil service lists, 1885-1900</li>
              <li>Pre-1900 official guides for prospective immigrants to Canada</li>
              <li>Selected speeches from statesmen such as Sir John A. Macdonald, Joseph Howe, Charles Tupper, Henri Bourassa, and others</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-footer">
          <a class="about-modern-detail-link" href="/catalog?f%5Bcollection_tsim_str%5D%5B%5D=Government+Publications+%7C+Publications+gouvernementales&amp;q=&amp;search_field=all_fields&amp;lang=<%= I18n.locale %>">Browse Government Publications</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--detail about-modern-card--detail-maps" aria-labelledby="canadiana-detail-maps-title">
        <header class="about-modern-detail-header">
          <h3 id="canadiana-detail-maps-title">Maps</h3>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-intro">
            The Maps collection currently contains nearly 22,000 Canadian maps digitized from the 1:50,000 scale National
            Topographic Series. The maps date from 1905 to 2012 and cover all of the Canadian provinces and territories.
            These maps depict in detail ground relief (landforms and terrain), drainage (lakes and rivers), forest cover,
            administrative areas, populated areas, transportation routes and facilities (including roads and railways), and
            other human-made features such as buildings, power lines and dams. The collection includes both colour and grayscale maps.
          </p>
          <div class="about-modern-detail-metadata" role="list" aria-label="Maps summary">
            <p class="about-modern-detail-size" role="listitem">
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-label">Size</span>
              <span class="about-modern-detail-size-value">Approximately 22,000 maps</span>
            </p>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">1905 to 2012</span>
            <span class="about-modern-detail-chip" role="listitem">National Topographic Series 1:50,000</span>
          </div>
          <p class="about-modern-detail-criteria">
            <strong>Selection criteria:</strong> The collection currently contains maps from the 1:50,000 scale National Topographic
            Series. It should be noted that the collection is not 100% complete and gaps will be filled in as missing maps become
            available. Maps from other series may be added in the future.
          </p>
        </header>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-grid">
          <section class="about-modern-detail-panel">
            <h4>Partnership and Access</h4>
            <p>
              The maps were digitized by McGill University Library and are presented here as the result of a partnership between
              McGill University Library and the Canadian Research Knowledge Network (CRKN). The Maps collection is the first
              large-scale addition of CRKN member content to the Canadiana collection.
            </p>
            <p>
              Portions of the 1:50,000 scale National Topographic Series Map Collection are also available through Scholars GeoPortal
              and Borealis, where maps have been georeferenced to create geospatial datasets for open use in research and historical
              analysis, with funding support from the University of Toronto Libraries, McGill University Libraries and Compute Ontario.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section class="about-modern-detail-panel">
            <h4>Contents</h4>
            <p>
              Maps from the 1:50,000 scale National Topographic Series, covering the years 1905 to 2012 and representing all
              Canadian provinces and territories.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="about-modern-detail-footer">
          <a class="about-modern-detail-link" href="/catalog?f%5Bcollection_tsim_str%5D%5B%5D=Maps+%7C+Cartes&amp;q=&amp;search_field=all_fields&amp;lang=<%= I18n.locale %>">Browse Maps</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="about-modern-block">
      <div class="about-modern-work-grid">
        <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--media">
          <img src="<%= asset_path('govpubs.jpg') %>" alt="Research workflow for Canadiana materials" loading="lazy">
        </article>
        <article class="about-modern-card about-modern-card--steps">
          <h2>How to Work with the Collection</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Start broad:</strong> Search across all fields to identify promising titles and themes.</li>
            <li><strong>Narrow fast:</strong> Use collection filters to focus on monographs, serials, maps, or government content.</li>
            <li><strong>Validate context:</strong> Review publication details, date ranges, and source metadata before citation.</li>
            <li><strong>Move to evidence:</strong> Open the full document to read, compare, and extract primary-source passages.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-modern-block" aria-labelledby="canadiana-faq-title">
      <div class="about-modern-block-head">
        <h2 id="canadiana-faq-title">Research Questions, Answered</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-modern-faq">
        <details open>
          <summary>What time period does the Canadiana Collection cover?</summary>
          <p>The collection includes materials from roughly 1500 to the present day, with especially strong coverage of pre-Confederation and early modern publication history.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How were materials selected for digitization?</summary>
          <p>Selection was guided by collection specialists and scholars, with emphasis on Canadian imprints, high-use historical sources, and materials that support broad interdisciplinary study.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I search inside documents?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Full-text and metadata search are available where text extraction exists, alongside title, creator, and subject searching.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is this collection suitable for teaching as well as research?</summary>
          <p>Yes. The range of formats and topics supports undergraduate instruction, graduate seminars, and advanced scholarly projects.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
